  "name": "KAPPA & LAMBDA FREE FREELITE URINE",
  "code": "1124",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"844\" data-end=\"1024\">\n<p data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"932\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Measures <strong data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"893\">free kappa and lambda light chains</strong> in urine to help diagnose and monitor:</span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"935\" data-end=\"1024\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"935\" data-end=\"957\">\n<p data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"957\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"957\">Multiple Myeloma</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"960\" data-end=\"999\">\n<p data-start=\"962\" data-end=\"999\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"962\" data-end=\"999\">Light Chain (Bence-Jones) Myeloma</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1002\" data-end=\"1024\">\n<p data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1024\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1024\">Amyloidosis (AL)</strong></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1127\">\n<p data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1127\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Abnormal levels or skewed ratio may indicate <strong data-start=\"1072\" data-end=\"1097\">monoclonal gammopathy</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1101\" data-end=\"1126\">plasma cell dyscrasia</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1128\" data-end=\"1244\">\n<p data-start=\"1130\" data-end=\"1244\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Often used with <strong data-start=\"1146\" data-end=\"1178\">serum free light chain assay</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1183\" data-end=\"1223\">urine protein electrophoresis (UPEP)</strong> for full evaluation.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
